3. Soliton (Schroedinger-Poisson ground state) against the smooth core (1 + x^2)^(-3/2)
  ground state eigenvalue 0.64953; half-density radius 1.2993; check against the known fit (1 + 0.091 (r/r_c)^2)^-8: max |ln d - ln form| over d above 1e-3: 0.061
  smooth core with the same half-density radius: ln(soliton/core) at x = 1, 2, 3, 4: -0.00, -0.63, -1.97, -3.76; soliton log slope at x = 2, 3: -4.18, -7.34; smooth core's limit -3
  so the gradient-plus-gravity minimum at fixed mass is the soliton, not (1 + x^2)^(-3/2). With a fixed oscillation frequency M_c r_c is constant, so S = rho_0 r_c goes as r_c^-3 and rises as the core shrinks
4. Baryon retention at L*: M_b/M200 at lg M_b 10.78 with EM1's relation
  lg M200 11.882 (Argon 11.94); M_b/M200 0.0791. EM1's M200 is the cold mass under FC1, so retention = (M_b/M200) / (Omega_b/Omega_c) = 0.417; Argon's 0.498 divides by 0.1595 against the cold mass
